%description:

Tcp.dropBeyondWindowEdge:rfc -- host2 takes the segment that ends beyond its window.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "true: as Linux (tcp_sequence()), a segment whose data ends beyond the
highest window edge offered is dropped whole, unless it starts within that edge and the
in-order receive queue is empty; false: the window test of RFC 9293 section 3.10.7.4, after
which only the receive buffer limits the data".

The classes: rfc (false, the default) and drop (true, the value of LinuxTcp). The code:
TcpConnection::isSegmentAcceptable() takes a segment that starts within the window (RFC 9293
section 3.10.7.4); with true, it drops a segment whose data ends beyond the highest edge
offered, unless the segment starts within that edge and the in-order receive queue is empty.
In that exception, the result is the same as with false, so no test can separate it. This test separates "rfc" from the other value.

Host under test: host2, with a receive buffer of 131072 bytes (precondition: the buffer does
not limit the data); host2 offers a window of 16384 bytes (advertisedWindow, a precondition), and its application
does not read. The tap writes 65535 into the window field of each segment of host2, so that
host1, which sends 50000 bytes, sends beyond the offer of host2. The 12th segment starts at
15928, within the window, and ends at 17376, beyond it. Observation: level 1, the highest ACK of host2 at 2 s acknowledges 12 segments, 17376 bytes:
the 12th segment starts within the window, and the buffer takes it.

%# parameter: Tcp.dropBeyondWindowEdge
%# class: rfc
%# value: false
%# key: *.host2.tcp.dropBeyondWindowEdge
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpDropBeyondWindowEdgeRfc")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host2").filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true").set("tcp.window", "65535")
                     .describe("each segment of host2: the window field 65535, so that host1 sends beyond the offer of host2"))
        .act(action().at(0.0).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().setAutoRead(false);
            app.socket().bind(1000);
            app.socket().listen();
        }))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                                        .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true")
                                        .captureMax("highestAck", "tcp.ackNo")
                                        .within(3.0)))
        .act(action().at(2.0)
                 .describe("the highest ACK of host2")
                 .assertModule("host2.tcp.conn-*", "{highestAck} == {isn} + 1 + 17376"));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpDropBeyondWindowEdgeRfc compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.dropBeyondWindowEdge = false    # the parameter under test
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 16384
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 50000B
*.host2.tcp.receiveBufferSize = 131072B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpDropBeyondWindowEdgeRfc: PASS
